Z||000000||darthtuttle||02-27-2000||11:15 PM||||So I've got a 88 Formula with &gt; 200,000 miles. I think it's time to rebuild it. The engine runs pretty well, a little oil on my plugs when I check them and a little smoke when I start the engine up, but it goes away (not sure this is oil, it could be h2o). Anyway, it's time to get rebuilt. <P>The tranny is another story. When I go in to third gear it grinds. It will always go, but unless I let the engine run all the way down going in to third it grinds. Oh yea, it's a Getrag/Muncie 282. The shifter cables and clutch are about a year and a half old. <P>The suspension I'm not to sure of. The car's been lowered by the previous owner (my father). I'm going to rip the entire thing out. I'm not sure the springs have the proper number of coils. I don't know much about the rest of the rest and figure if I'm pulling the entire thing apart, might as well do it all, so...<P>When I rebuild the engine I'd like to hook it up. What mods can I look at to get some more performance out of it? I'm more interested in torque then hp. I like lots of it in the low end, and lots of it all the way up. I don't need a drag racer.<P>The tranny I don't know much about what I can do to. Is there anything I can do for it.<P>As for the suspension I like it low and hard. Any ideas? Oh, how many coils should I have in the springs?<P>Thanks for the ideas. I hope to have fun with this car.h||||reg||5
